With an angered deity it's no longer about quantity.  It is now about
quality.

> As for the angered god, it's a bit worse. You should consult the
> spoiler http://www.nethack.de/spoiler/appeasement.txt to check which
> sacrifices are worthy. If a sacrifice is not worthy you will have a
> "feeling of inadequacy" and nothing will happen. Since you only
> angered your god by one point, one worthy sacrifice will be enough,
> but they may be a bit though for you. Also, you will need a co-aligned
> altar to do that.

If you don't want to read the spoiler here's a simple system - If
the message you get is a "feeling of inadequacy" then that type
of corpse wasn't mean enough to satisfy your angry god.  No
matter how many of that type you offer it will have no effect at
all, and no monster less mean will help either.

What to do is offer progressively more mean corpse types
until they are no longer inadequate.  It may take several cycles
of finding a meaner monster type, luring it near the altar, killing
it, offering it until you find a type mean enough to cure the
anger.

> In any case, don't pray until you appease your god.

Yup.  And you'll need to find a co-aligned altar to work at.  Trying
it at a cross-aligned altar is a bad idea.


